{
  "result": "If I had a magic wand and could only change one thing, I wouldn't fix a single problem - I'd fix how we *approach* every problem.\n\nI would make empathy our default setting.\n\nNot just being nice to each other, but truly being able to feel, for even a moment, what it's like to walk in another person's shoes. To understand their fears, their history, why they believe what they believe.\n\nI think so much of the hurt in the world - loneliness, division, cruelty, even wars - comes from fear and misunderstanding. From feeling so unseen ourselves that we can't make space to really see someone else.\n\nIf our first instinct was curiosity instead of judgment, and compassion instead of defensiveness, I think everything else would start to cascade. We'd still have disagreements and huge challenges, but we'd solve them *together* instead of against each other. People who feel seen and safe can be so incredibly creative, kind, and brave.\n\nBasically, I'd make everyone feel secure enough to be kind, and understood enough to be understanding.\n\nIt's a big one, I know. What about you - what would your one change be?",
